  "name": "Satchel Courier",
  "description": "The Traders' courier: small and fast, two standard 2 m containers in a bay sunk into its middle, open to the sky so a dock's crane lifts each one straight out. A glass cockpit and a crew cab forward (bunks, a head, a galley, an airlock over the boarding shaft), a passage down each side of the bay to engineering, and a big drive nacelle on a pylon to each side of it. Lift jets and legs under the cab and engineering set it down; attitude jets at both ends and on the nacelles' noses move it about.",
